  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759121,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 10,000 Meters: A Perilous Descent\n\nPlunge into the icy abyss in *10,000 Meters*, a chilling survival simulation for the Commodore 64. After your small plane suffers engine failure high above the Swiss Alps, you must guide your pilot to safety in a desperate, freefall descent. \n\nThe game combines stunning (for the time) graphics with a tense, real-time gameplay loop. You control the pilot's movements, adjusting his body position to steer and manage his fall speed.  Carefully navigate treacherous terrain – jagged peaks, dense forests, and icy ravines – while battling the elements.  Altitude, wind speed, and even snow conditions impact your survival.\n\nSuccess depends on quick reflexes and strategic decision-making.  You must utilize the pilot's limited equipment, like a parachute, at the opportune moment to avoid certain death.  *10,000 Meters* offers a unique and heart-pounding experience, testing your skills against the unforgiving power of nature. Can you survive the fall?"
    },
